  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🐈‍⬛ Black Cat Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Black cat names, and Halloween names for any cat or dog: spooky, cute, gothic or good enough to eat."
    },
    "intro": "Black cats have been witches' companions in folklore for centuries, and a good black cat name leans into it: Soot, Onyx, Nightshade, Lord Inkwell. This **black cat name generator** also names any cat or dog for Halloween, in four styles, with a costume if you like.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Black cats, witches and luck",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Witches' cats:</strong> in the European witch scares of the 1500s and 1600s, cats, and black cats in particular, were said to be witches' familiars. That's where the Halloween black cat comes from.</li><li><strong>Lucky or unlucky?</strong> It depends where you are. In Britain a black cat crossing your path has long been a sign of good luck, and a black cat at a wedding is a good omen. In much of the United States it's the other way round.</li><li><strong>Black Cat Day:</strong> Cats Protection, the UK cat charity, holds National Black Cat Day every year on 27 October. It says black and black-and-white cats often wait longer than others to find a home, so October is a good time to adopt one.</li><li><strong>Black dogs too:</strong> English folklore has its own ghostly black dogs, like Black Shuck of East Anglia and the Barghest of Yorkshire, which is why the dog names have a few of their own.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Picking a name your pet will answer to",
